as_results=false and no publication in any source (status UNKNOWN since 2017). Eligible trial, NO extractable result anywhere -- a genuine evidence gap (results-unavailable), not a matcher or access-tier failure. Stays a corticosteroids-cap completeness caveat.</span></li><li><strong>FISSH</strong> &rarr; balanced-crystalloids-vs-saline-mortality: <code>NOT_FOUND</code> <span class='muted'>zero linked publications on CT.gov (per read-only session); no extractable result. Results-unavailable reach limit.</span></li><li><strong>SONIA</strong> &rarr; corticosteroids-cap-mortality: <code>UNVERIFIED</code> <span class='muted'>name-only in the audit record; no confirmed PMID. Requires author/name search with uncertain yield (several likely small/non-English/registry-only). Recorded as a structural reach limit pending an identifier; not asserted eligible. [CONFIRMED reach limit: a clean known-item search for &quot;Nafae ... severe CAP randomized&quot; returns 0 -- these need the DEFERRED concept-query/reference-seeding search rebuild, not a per-trial fetch. This is a search-completeness gap, correctly documented.]</span></li><li><strong>McHardy/El-Ghamrawy/Mikami/Sabry/Nafae/Snijders (corticosteroid-CAP set)</strong> &rarr; corticosteroids-cap-mortality: <code>UNVERIFIED</code> <span class='muted'>name-only in the audit record; no confirmed PMID. Requires author/name search with uncertain yield (several likely small/non-English/registry-only). Recorded as a structural reach limit pending an identifier; not asserted eligible. [CONFIRMED reach limit: a clean known-item search for &quot;Nafae ... severe CAP randomized&quot; returns 0 -- these need the DEFERRED concept-query/reference-seeding search rebuild, not a per-trial fetch. This is a search-completeness gap, correctly documented.]</span></li><li><strong>Sarzaeem</strong> &rarr; corticosteroids-covid19-mortality: <code>UNVERIFIED</code> <span class='muted'>name-only in the audit record; no confirmed PMID. Requires author/name search with uncertain yield (several likely small/non-English/registry-only). Recorded as a structural reach limit pending an identifier; not asserted eligible.</span></li><li><strong>iv-iron recurrent strand (AFFIRM-AHF + IRONMAN)</strong> &rarr; iv-iron-hfref-hosp: <code>STRAND_BUILT_ENDPOINT_SPLIT_CORRECTED</code> <span class='muted'>BUILT as three declared strands (docs/iv_iron_strands.json). CORRECTION: the &#x27;recurrent strand&#x27; AFFIRM-AHF 0.74 + IRONMAN 0.82 -&gt; 0.783 was CROSS-ENDPOINT -- it paired AFFIRM-AHF&#x27;s HF-hosp-ALONE rate (0.74) with IRONMAN&#x27;s HF-hosp+CV-death COMPOSITE rate (0.82). The compatibility key refuses that pool. The endpoint-clean strands are B (HF-hosp alone: AFFIRM-AHF 0.74 + FAIR-HF2 0.80 -&gt; 0.765, HKSJ 0.232-2.522, crosses null) and C (composite: AFFIRM-AHF 0.79 + IRONMAN 0.82 -&gt; 0.807, HKSJ 0.281-2.312, crosses null). [CI CORRECTION: the earlier 0.64-0.92 / 0.69-0.95 were z-based common-effect sensitivities mislabelled as the registered result; under the registered PM+HKSJ method at k=2 (t(1)=12.7) both strands cross the null.] That the old 0.78 &#x27;reproduced the published 0.77&#x27; is not reassurance -- the published two-trial meta-analysis makes the SAME cross-endpoint conflation.</span></li><li><strong>Nafae</strong> &rarr; corticosteroids-cap-mortality: <code>NOT_FOUND</code> <span class='muted'>clean known-item search returns 0; needs the deferred concept-query/reference-seeding rebuild. Search-completeness gap.</span></li></ul></p></div><div class='banner'><h2>Participant-flow acquisition for the attrition domain (D3) &mdash; data landed, judgement pending</h2><p><strong>Of 101 pooled trials across 32 topics: 59 have usable per-arm participant flow</strong> on ClinicalTrials.gov (started / completed / not-completed with verbatim non-completion reasons). The rest are not a failure to fetch but a boundary of the source: <strong>22 have no NCT at all</strong> (older or non-US trials the registry cannot describe) and <strong>20 have an NCT but posted no structured results</strong> to CT.gov. The non-completion REASON is carried verbatim; attrition is never derived from started-minus-completed (the AMPLITUDE-O rule).</p><p><strong>24 of 32 topics could have a real D3 judgement</strong> once judgement runs (&ge;1 pooled trial with usable flow); <strong>18</strong> have usable flow for every pooled trial. No D3 judgement is assigned in this pass &mdash; the field is populated and rendered; the judgement is a separate, fresh pass.</p></div><div class='banner'><h2>iv-iron HF-hospitalisation: declared strands (topic-page and index render the same artefact)</h2><div class='banner'><h3>Declared strands (the single pool is suppressed; these are the endpoint-clean decompositions)</h3><p>Strands A and B measure the SAME endpoint (HF hospitalisation) two incompatible ways -- first-event HR (CONFIRM-HF) vs recurrent rate ratio (AFFIRM-AHF + FAIR-HF2). A hazard ratio of the first event and a rate ratio of all events are not the same quantity and cannot be pooled; the single-pool primary is therefore correctly suppressed. The strands below are the honest decomposition.</p><ul><li><strong>Strand A</strong> — First-event hazard ratio (time to first HF hospitalisation) [<code>FIRST_EVENT_RATIO</code>]: CONFIRM-HF 0.39 (HR), k=1 (single trial)</li><li><strong>Strand B</strong> — Recurrent-event rate ratio, HF hospitalisation ALONE [<code>RATE</code>]: pooled 0.765 (0.232–2.522), k=2, HKSJ/PM &tau;&sup2;=0.0, <strong>crosses null</strong> <span class='note'>[common-effect sensitivity 0.765 (0.636–0.919), NOT the registered result]</span></li><li><strong>Strand C</strong> — Recurrent-event rate ratio, HF hospitalisation + CV death COMPOSITE [<code>RATE</code>]: pooled 0.807 (0.281–2.312), k=2, HKSJ/PM &tau;&sup2;=0.0, <strong>crosses null</strong> <span class='note'>[common-effect sensitivity 0.807 (0.686–0.949), NOT the registered result]</span></li><li><strong>Strand D</strong> — Participant-level risk (patients with &gt;=1 HF hospitalisation) [<code>PARTICIPANT_RISK</code>]: CONFIRM-HF 0.39 (RR (crude)), k=1 (single trial)</li></ul><p><strong>Refused cross-endpoint pool:</strong> The recurrent-event rate ratios do NOT form one pool. A pool of AFFIRM-AHF&#x27;s HF-hosp-ALONE rate (0.74) with IRONMAN&#x27;s HF-hosp+CV-death COMPOSITE rate (0.82) crosses the endpoint dimension of the compatibility key. If forced it would be 0.783 (0.275-2.233) -- this is the 0.783 figure previously treated as the recurrent strand; it mixes endpoints and is refused, not published. — <code>REFUSED -- endpoint mismatch (HF-hosp alone vs composite)</code>.</p><p class='note'>Every effect source-verified; intervals from the canonical engine. The compatibility key keeps strands apart; a cross-strand pool is refused, not computed.</p></div></div><div class='banner'><h2>Search recall, regression corpus (not prospective validation): <strong>18 of 20</strong> known-eligible trials recalled unaided</h2><p>Measured 2026-09-15T18:04Z on the 5 named regression-corpus topics in <code>registry/regression_recall_topics.json</code>. All 32 current corpus topics are disqualified as held-out because they have been exposed through audits, URLs, commit history, or regression work; prospective validation will use topics held outside the repository and revealed only when that run begins. Denominator per topic = pooled primary trials + eligible-declared-absent trials with a PMID. Engine pinned at <code>b8c47f64bbc7</code>; any change to the engine must publish a new regression-corpus row here before it can land.</p><table><tr><th>topic</th><th>source state</th><th>boolean hits</th><th>recalled</th></tr><tr><td>denosumab-vertebral-fracture</td><td><code>RAN_OK</code></td><td>165</td><td>1 of 1</td></tr><tr><td>pcsk9-mace</td><td><code>RAN_OK</code></td><td>519</td><td>2 of 2</td></tr><tr><td>statins-primary-prevention-elderly</td><td><code>RAN_OK</code></td><td>643</td><td>4 of 4</td